  "notes": [
    "Intel IR models consume BGR values 0..255 in NCHW layout; raw eye-state ONNX consumes BGR normalised as (pixel-127)/255.",
    "Eye-state class order follows official C++ demo: index1=open. Verified on upstream example images: 1.png and3.png visibly open with p(open)=1.0;2.png visibly closed with p(open)=0.0000087. Model README reverses class names.",
    "Gaze API convention is x=image right, y=image up, z=towards camera. Model z is negated to make frontal gaze positive; x/y match official demo arrows. A learned direction is not a calibrated fixation or attention probability."
  ],
